    {
      "id": "get-num-uv-layers",
      "name": "GetNumUVLayers",
      "category": "MeshDescriptionUVsToDynamicMesh",
      "signature": "GetNumUVLayers(Target, Input Mesh Description)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FMeshDescriptionUVsToDynamicMesh*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Input Mesh Description",
          "type": "FMeshDescription*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Int",
      "docs": "Converter that gives a specific UV layer of a provided mesh description and turns it into a flat\nFDynamicMesh, with vertices corresponding to UV elements, and their positions corresponding to\nthose elements' UV coordinate values. The triangle id's in the dynamic mesh will correspond to\noriginal triangles of the mesh.\nThe converter can also bake back such a dynamic mesh to an existing mesh description UV layer\nafter the dynamic mesh has been modified. The important part is that the triangle IDs continue\nto correspond to each other. This means that while welding/splitting vertices in the dynamic\nmesh is ok, adding or removing triangles is not.\nThe converter prefers shared UVs when they are available, though it will populate instanced\nUVs as well on the way back."
    },
